# Secret-shaped strings. One POSIX extended regex per line; blank lines and
# lines starting with # are ignored. Matched case-sensitively, byte-wise
# (LC_ALL=C), line by line. Read by src/secret-scan.ts, so keep each pattern
# valid in both POSIX ERE and JavaScript RegExp syntax.
#
# hmcts/cft-workspace keeps a twin copy at scripts/lib/secret-patterns, read by
# its scripts/lib/_secret_scan.sh (the knowledge-sweep flow, which does not use
# this package). The two must not diverge: if they do, this client and the
# knowledge sweep disagree about what a secret looks like.
eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}\.
gh[pousr]_[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}
AccountKey=
BEGIN (RSA|EC|OPENSSH|PRIVATE)[ ]
(client_secret|api[_-]?key|password)["':= ]+[A-Za-z0-9/+_-]{16,}
ABSK[A-Za-z0-9+/]{40,}
bedrock-api-key-[A-Za-z0-9+/]{40,}
